": null, "comments": 5, "created_at": "2021-02-27T13:32:06Z", "updated_at": "2024-07-25T12:57:03Z", "closed_at": "2024-07-25T12:57:03Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "WTF is wrong with this picture, imagine this in an advert; \"commercially sold open source software\"... just ponder on that for a while...\r\n\r\nQuote from RigPi homepage; \"Software for RigPi will be available on GitHub as a free, open-source download. Add your own features to RSS!\"\r\n\r\nSo, still boosting on the M*J site about being \"open source\" and \"free\" blah blah blah, are we? BS!\r\n\r\nAnd all links on the net bragging about the same thing, open this, source that, free nada...!\r\nSimple truth ? MFJ would not give away a dust-rat from the floor for free, let alone a piece of \"open source\" software.\r\nNot as long as they still can make a single cent from it, and would rather torch and burn their entire stock before giving a\r\nsingle piece of anything away free. \r\n\r\nYes folks, that´s the sad truth. And waiting here on GitHub are us morons who still hope the will obey the promises made \r\nGitHub, the original creator of the software (before greedy MFJ got their fingers on it) and all others who knows what \"open source\" means.\r\nMaybe the good folks at MFJ are poor at English ? \r\nMaybe Git Hub should kick them out for obviously NOT sharing anything?\r\nKick them out for charging customers for \"free open source\" software ?\r\nFor using \"open source\" as a major salespoint and using the name \"Git Hub\" in their promo as well, when in fact NOTHING is shared here or elsewhere?\r\n\r\nWell, perhaps MFJ is a well paying customer, which I am not, so let them keep their empty account, don´t rock the boat?\r\n\r\nSeriously Git Hub, you have many eyes on you. You´ve done this before. \r\nKick them the heck out, since they still (AFTER 3 YEARS!) share nothing and breach their contract of intent and the whole idea of open source I might add.\r\n\r\n@ all of Ham community, write about this idiocracy, talk about \"MFJ open source RigPi\", spread the word around the world. \r\nThis is a total disgrace and a \"spit in the face\" (again) on the idea of open source in general, and on all of the thousands \"follow the leader - don´t speak too loud - we´ll behave oh Lord of the Antennaswitch master, sire\" -ham's in general.\r\nBut enough is enough.\r\n\r\nMFJ is ripping you off making you have to pay dearly for what they call \"free\" (duh?) \"open source\" software\r\n(yeah, the OS they use AND MAKE YOUR PAY FOR on ready-made SD-cards is both free and open) and this is just bleedin´ scandalous. Outrageous. In Swedish; \"helt åt helvete\" (Google will translate that one for you).\r\n\r\nI have no illusions regarding MFJ to anytime before the second coming of Christ suddenly changing their minds \r\nor me by this text at GitHub making any difference in any way, shape or form.\r\nBut I am a bit curious, will Git Hub act upon MFJ or me and my little post here?\r\nLet´s see how long this post will be up before someone with money makes it disappear...\r\n\r\nBtw, there are many, many other FREE and true open source solutions here on Git Hub and elsewhere on the web that does the same thing. It just ticks me off when big corporations p-in-your-face-people promise gold and prove to be lying to a whole community and, frankly my dear, just does´nt give a damn about it! (oh btw, that´s the same community that for some incomprehensible reason still keeps them in business none the less).\r\n\r\nThis is a scandal and intentional damage upon all that open source stands for and was ever meant to be, and perhaps yet another signal of it´s demise.\r\n\r\n73s and greetings from Sweden!\r\n ", "closed_by": {"login": "hlnurse", "id": 29